<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#f5f8fc">
  <title>PrivateChat | Private Android messaging</title>
  <meta name="description" content="PrivateChat is a direct, encrypted text chat project for two Android phones.">

  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --ink: #15283a;
      --muted: #5c7082;
      --blue: #2563eb;
      --paper: #f5f8fc;
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--paper);
      color: var(--ink);
      font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    }

    .wrap {
      width: min(100% - 36px, 1040px);
      margin: auto;
    }

    nav {
      height: 74px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
    }

    .brand {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: -.3px;
    }

    .mark {
      width: 35px;
      height: 35px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: var(--blue);
      color: #fff;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      font-weight: 800;
    }

    .badge {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: #2253ab;
      background: #e7efff;
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 6px 11px;
      font-weight: 700;
    }

    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.05fr .95fr;
      gap: 32px;
      align-items: center;
      padding: 42px 0 28px;
    }

    .kicker {
      font-size: 12px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 1.7px;
      font-weight: 800;
      color: var(--blue);
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(42px, 8vw, 72px);
      line-height: 1.02;
      letter-spacing: -3px;
      margin: 14px 0 18px;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 18px;
      color: var(--muted);
      max-width: 560px;
    }

    .note {
      font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-top: 20px;
    }

    .phone {
      max-width: 360px;
      width: 100%;
      justify-self: center;
      background: #fff;
      border: 8px solid #182b3c;
      border-radius: 34px;
      padding: 17px;
      box-shadow: 0 24px 60px #19324a20;
    }

    .phone-top {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      color: #8291a0;
      font-size: 12px;
      margin-bottom: 17px;
    }

    .status {
      background: #f3f7fb;
      border-radius: 13px;
      padding: 12px 13px;
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .dot {
      display: inline-block;
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: #f4a62a;
      margin-right: 7px;
    }

    .panel {
      border: 1px solid #e7edf3;
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 15px;
      margin: 10px 0;
    }

    .panel h3 {
      font-size: 15px;
      margin: 0 0 5px;
    }

    .small {
      font-size: 12px;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0;
    }

    .code {
      color: var(--blue);
      font-size: 19px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      margin: 12px 0 4px;
    }

    .ip {
      font-size: 11px;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .fake-button {
      display: block;
      text-align: center;
      color: white;
      background: var(--blue);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 8px;
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-top: 10px;
    }

    .section {
      padding: 24px 0;
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 26px;
      letter-spacing: -.7px;
      margin: 0 0 14px;
    }

    .grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 14px;
    }

    .card {
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid #e7edf3;
      border-radius: 17px;
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 7px;
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .callout {
      background: #eaf2ff;
      border-radius: 18px;
      padding: 21px 23px;
      margin: 12px 0 34px;
    }

    .callout strong {
      display: block;
      margin-bottom: 5px;
    }

    .callout p {
      margin: 0;
      color: #425970;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    footer {
      border-top: 1px solid #e1e8ef;
      padding: 20px 0 32px;
      color: #748393;
      font-size: 12px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .hero {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 20px;
        padding-top: 30px;
      }

      .phone {
        max-width: 390px;
      }

      .grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      h1 {
        letter-spacing: -2px;
      }

      .wrap {
        width: min(100% - 28px, 1040px);
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav>
      <div class="brand">
        <span class="mark">P</span>
        <span>PrivateChat</span>
      </div>
      <span class="badge">Android project - v1</span>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">Private messaging for Android</div>
          <h1>Chat directly.<br>Keep it private.</h1>
          <p class="lead">
            A small Android project for sending encrypted text between two
            phones, without accounts or a message database.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            This page is a project preview. It is not the chat app itself.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="phone" aria-label="Illustration of the Android app screen">
          <div class="phone-top">
            <span>9:41</span>
            <span>Wi-Fi&nbsp;&nbsp; 100%</span>
          </div>

          <div class="status">
            <span class="dot"></span>Not connected
          </div>

          <div class="panel">
            <h3>Create a room</h3>
            <p class="small">Share the room code and local Wi-Fi address.</p>
            <div class="code">7J4K 9M2Q 8V6T</div>
            <div class="ip">Local IP: 192.168.1.24 - Port 45678</div>
            <span class="fake-button">Start hosting</span>
          </div>

          <div class="panel">
            <h3>Join a room</h3>
            <p class="small">Enter the host address and room code.</p>
            <span class="fake-button">Connect directly</span>
          </div>

          <div class="panel">
            <h3>Messages</h3>
            <p class="small">Messages stay in memory while the app is open.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2 class="section-title">How the project works</h2>
        <div class="grid">
          <article class="card">
            <h3>01 - Create a room</h3>
            <p>One phone hosts and shows a temporary Room Code and its local network address.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>02 - Connect directly</h3>
            <p>The second phone enters the address and code to connect over a direct TCP socket.</p>
          </article>

          <article class="card">
            <h3>03 - Send encrypted text</h3>
            <p>The Android app protects messages in transit. It does not save chat history to a server.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="callout">
        <strong>Network limits</strong>
        <p>
          Same-Wi-Fi connections are the simplest. Internet connections require
          the host phone to be reachable from outside its network. This project
          has no relay server, and this web page does not send chat messages.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      PrivateChat - Open the Android project in Android Studio to build and install the app.
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
